  "worked_solution": "Since we are given both the derivative of the curve ${r}^{\u2032}(t)$ and the derivative of the unit tangent ${T}^{\u2032}(t)$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\n\u03ba(t)=\\frac{\u2016{T}^{\u2032}(t)\u2016}{\u2016{r}^{\u2032}(t)\u2016}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the magnitudes of ${r}^{\u2032}(t)$ and ${T}^{\u2032}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u2016{T}^{\u2032}(t)\u2016 & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t)}^{2}+{(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t)}^{2}+(-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(\\frac{3}{4}+\\frac{1}{4}){cos}^{2}\u2061t+{sin}^{2}\u2061t} \\\\  & =1 \\\\ \u2016{r}^{\u2032}(t)\u2016 & =\\sqrt{3{sin}^{2}\u2061t+{sin}^{2}\u2061t+4{cos}^{2}\u2061t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4({sin}^{2}\u2061t+{cos}^{2}\u2061t)} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u03ba(t) & =\\frac{\u2016{T}^{\u2032}(t)\u2016}{\u2016{r}^{\u2032}(t)\u2016}=\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
